  "Area": "Unclassified",
  "Number": 13,
  "Question": "At a party, each man danced with exactly three women and each woman danced with exactly two men. Twelve men attended the party. How many women attended the party?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(8\\)",
    "B": "\\(12\\)",
    "C": "\\(16\\)",
    "D": "\\(18\\)",
    "E": "\\(24\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Count the man-woman pairs who danced together, counting each partnership once. From the men’s side, the \\(12\\) men each had \\(3\\) partners, giving\n\\[\n12\\cdot3=36\n\\]\npartnerships.\n\nFrom the women’s side, each woman accounts for exactly \\(2\\) partnerships. These are the same partnerships counted from their other members, so the number of women is\n\\[\n36\\div2=\\boxed{18}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\mathrm{D}\\).",
